        "answer": "# Gross Domestic Product (GDP)\n\nGDP is the market value of all the final goods and services produced within the domestic territory of a country during a year. It includes all production by national residents or non-residents, regardless of ownership, and is valued at market prices.\n\n$GDP_{MP} = C + I + G + (X - M)$\n\nWhere:\n*   **C** = Consumption expenditure\n*   **I** = Investment expenditure\n*   **G** = Government expenditure\n*   **(X - M)** = Net exports (Exports - Imports)\n\nGDP can also be expressed at factor cost:\n$GDP_{FC} = GDP_{MP} - NIT$\nWhere **NIT** = Net Indirect Taxes (Indirect Taxes - Subsidies). \n\n**📘 Source:** NCERT Class 11 Economics • Gdp"
      },
